1
00:00:01,460 --> 00:00:02,450
One thousand, two hundred and sixty-five.

2
00:00:02,500 --> 00:00:05,950
That's how many Australians drove away
in what they were told was a brand-new

3
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:11,370
2026 BYD only to find out it
had actually been built in 2025.

4
00:00:11,420 --> 00:00:13,770
A whole model year older
than the paperwork said.

5
00:00:13,820 --> 00:00:17,070
A whole year of depreciation
they never agreed to pay for.

6
00:00:17,120 --> 00:00:19,490
BYD called it an administrative error.

7
00:00:19,540 --> 00:00:21,770
Its first offer was
eleven hundred dollars.

8
00:00:21,820 --> 00:00:22,710
Owners said no.

9
00:00:22,760 --> 00:00:23,750
They went to the media.

10
00:00:23,800 --> 00:00:24,430
They pushed back.

11
00:00:24,480 --> 00:00:25,790
And within weeks,

12
00:00:25,840 --> 00:00:29,790
the offer more than tripled to thirty-five
hundred dollars plus a full refund

13
00:00:29,840 --> 00:00:34,250
or a swap for a genuine 2026
car for anyone who wanted it.

14
00:00:34,300 --> 00:00:35,690
That's not the only one.

15
00:00:35,740 --> 00:00:40,250
In 2026, a Victorian buyer took a dealer
all the way to the Supreme Court over

16
00:00:40,300 --> 00:00:42,870
a rusty car and won a full refund.

17
00:00:42,920 --> 00:00:46,170
The car industry's own dealers have
admitted the system is failing.

18
00:00:46,220 --> 00:00:49,130
And the government has agreed to hit
businesses with penalties when they

19
00:00:49,180 --> 00:00:51,250
refuse to fix what they sold you.

20
00:00:51,300 --> 00:00:55,170
Aussie drivers are fighting back against
faulty new cars and they're winning.

21
00:00:55,220 --> 00:00:58,450
In this video, I'll show
you the real 2026 cases,

22
00:00:58,500 --> 00:01:00,210
why it's still so hard to get a refund,

23
00:01:00,260 --> 00:01:04,050
and the exact steps you can take if
your new car turns out to be a dud.

24
00:01:04,100 --> 00:01:06,330
Because most Aussies
don't know their rights.

25
00:01:06,380 --> 00:01:07,980
And the car industry knows it.

26
00:01:08,423 --> 00:01:10,763
First, something that
surprises a lot of people.

27
00:01:10,813 --> 00:01:14,033
Australia doesn't have a
specific lemon law for cars.

28
00:01:14,083 --> 00:01:15,393
Some American states do.

29
00:01:15,443 --> 00:01:16,193
We don't.

30
00:01:16,243 --> 00:01:19,053
What we have instead is the
Australian Consumer Law.

31
00:01:19,103 --> 00:01:23,113
Under it, everything you buy from a phone
to a sixty-thousand-dollar ute comes

32
00:01:23,163 --> 00:01:25,313
with automatic consumer guarantees.

33
00:01:25,363 --> 00:01:27,213
It has to be of acceptable quality.

34
00:01:27,263 --> 00:01:28,713
It has to be fit for purpose.

35
00:01:28,763 --> 00:01:30,753
It has to match the
description you were given.

36
00:01:30,803 --> 00:01:32,893
And it has to last a reasonable time.

37
00:01:32,943 --> 00:01:35,573
That last part matters more
than most people realise.

38
00:01:35,623 --> 00:01:37,753
The guarantees don't stop
when the warranty stops.

39
00:01:37,803 --> 00:01:41,473
If a major part fails earlier than it
reasonably should for the price you

40
00:01:41,523 --> 00:01:45,633
paid, you can still have rights, even
after the factory warranty has run out.

41
00:01:45,683 --> 00:01:47,113
If your car has a minor fault,

42
00:01:47,163 --> 00:01:50,093
you're entitled to a free
repair within a reasonable time.

43
00:01:50,143 --> 00:01:53,893
If it has a major failure or the same
problem keeps coming back you can choose

44
00:01:53,943 --> 00:01:55,933
a refund or a replacement.

45
00:01:55,983 --> 00:01:58,753
And the key part: these
rights cannot be excluded,

46
00:01:58,803 --> 00:02:01,333
restricted or changed by any business.

47
00:02:01,383 --> 00:02:02,473
Not by the dealer.

48
00:02:02,523 --> 00:02:03,773
Not by the car maker.

49
00:02:03,823 --> 00:02:06,293
Not by the small print on
the contract you signed.

50
00:02:06,343 --> 00:02:08,003
So what counts as a major failure?

51
00:02:08,053 --> 00:02:10,023
According to the ACCC's guidance,

52
00:02:10,073 --> 00:02:14,073
a fault is major if you wouldn't have
bought the car had you known about it.

53
00:02:14,123 --> 00:02:17,453
Or if the car is significantly different
from the description or the demo you

54
00:02:17,503 --> 00:02:18,253
were shown.

55
00:02:18,303 --> 00:02:21,713
Or if it's substantially unfit for
its normal purpose and can't be fixed

56
00:02:21,763 --> 00:02:23,973
easily or within a reasonable time.

57
00:02:24,023 --> 00:02:25,253
Or if it's unsafe.

58
00:02:25,303 --> 00:02:25,893
In real life,

59
00:02:25,943 --> 00:02:29,193
that could be an engine that has
to be replaced in the first year.

60
00:02:29,243 --> 00:02:32,083
A transmission that keeps
failing after repeated repairs.

61
00:02:32,133 --> 00:02:34,953
Electrical faults that leave
you stranded again and again.

62
00:02:35,003 --> 00:02:39,113
Or a car that spends more time in
the workshop than in your driveway.

63
00:02:39,163 --> 00:02:40,913
And there's one more important idea:

64
00:02:40,963 --> 00:02:44,053
a series of minor faults can
add up to a major failure.

65
00:02:44,103 --> 00:02:46,573
If your car keeps going
back for different problems,

66
00:02:46,623 --> 00:02:49,213
and together they mean you wouldn't
have bought it had you known,

67
00:02:49,263 --> 00:02:52,853
you can argue you have a major failure
even if no single fault would be enough

68
00:02:52,903 --> 00:02:53,833
on its own.

69
00:02:53,883 --> 00:02:54,893
It sounds simple.

70
00:02:54,943 --> 00:02:57,393
So why do so many owners
end up in a fight?

71
00:02:57,443 --> 00:03:00,123
Let's look at what's
actually happened in 2026.

72
00:03:02,224 --> 00:03:04,826
Case number one: BYD and
the wrong build year.

73
00:03:04,876 --> 00:03:06,566
In July 2026,

74
00:03:06,616 --> 00:03:10,826
the ABC and the Sydney Morning Herald
reported that BYD had sold cars to

75
00:03:10,876 --> 00:03:16,266
Australian customers as 2026 models when
they had actually been built in 2025.

76
00:03:16,316 --> 00:03:21,486
The affected models included the Atto
3, the Sealion 8 and the Shark 6 ute.

77
00:03:21,536 --> 00:03:25,266
BYD said around 3,800 vehicles
had been incorrectly listed,

78
00:03:25,316 --> 00:03:30,486
and roughly 1,200 of them had already
been sold or allocated to customers.

79
00:03:30,536 --> 00:03:34,286
BYD's explanation was that it had used
the date the cars left the factory,

80
00:03:34,336 --> 00:03:37,746
rather than the date they were
built, in sales contracts.

81
00:03:37,796 --> 00:03:41,446
BYD Australia's public relations director
called it an administrative error

82
00:03:41,496 --> 00:03:43,346
and said there was no deceit.

83
00:03:43,396 --> 00:03:44,766
To be fair to BYD,

84
00:03:44,816 --> 00:03:46,606
the specifications of
the cars were the same,

85
00:03:46,656 --> 00:03:50,666
and the correct build date was in the
vehicle identification number all along.

86
00:03:50,716 --> 00:03:52,506
But here's why owners were angry.

87
00:03:52,556 --> 00:03:55,026
A car's build year
affects its resale value.

88
00:03:55,076 --> 00:03:59,006
Erin Turner from the Consumer Policy
Research Centre said these owners had

89
00:03:59,056 --> 00:04:01,766
effectively taken on an
extra year of depreciation,

90
00:04:01,816 --> 00:04:04,716
and warned they could be seriously
out of pocket when they sold.

91
00:04:04,766 --> 00:04:08,466
The Insurance Council of Australia
even advised affected owners to contact

92
00:04:08,516 --> 00:04:11,346
their insurers, because the
error could affect their cover.

93
00:04:11,396 --> 00:04:14,726
BYD's first offer was $1,100.

94
00:04:14,776 --> 00:04:16,726
Owners didn't accept that quietly.

95
00:04:16,776 --> 00:04:20,146
Within days, BYD added the
option of a full refund.

96
00:04:20,196 --> 00:04:24,646
Then it raised the payment to
$3,500 and made it retrospective,

97
00:04:24,696 --> 00:04:27,626
so owners who had already accepted the
lower amount would get the difference

98
00:04:27,676 --> 00:04:28,186
too.

99
00:04:28,236 --> 00:04:32,466
Owners could also swap their car for
a like-for-like vehicle built in 2026,

100
00:04:32,516 --> 00:04:34,946
with BYD covering the costs.

101
00:04:34,996 --> 00:04:35,986
By late July,

102
00:04:36,036 --> 00:04:39,246
BYD said around seventy-two per cent
of owners had taken the payment,

103
00:04:39,296 --> 00:04:43,246
and more than 350 had chosen
a refund or a replacement.

104
00:04:43,296 --> 00:04:45,186
That's what fighting back looks like.

105
00:04:45,236 --> 00:04:48,566
The owners who spoke up didn't just
get a better deal for themselves.

106
00:04:48,616 --> 00:04:51,196
They got a better deal
for every owner affected.

107
00:04:52,764 --> 00:04:56,211
Case number two: the rusty car that
went all the way to the Supreme Court.

108
00:04:56,261 --> 00:04:58,791
In a case published in March 2026,

109
00:04:58,841 --> 00:05:01,991
a Victorian buyer discovered that the
car she'd bought from a dealer had

110
00:05:02,041 --> 00:05:03,351
serious rust.

111
00:05:03,401 --> 00:05:06,371
The tribunal found it was a clear
breach of the consumer guarantee of

112
00:05:06,421 --> 00:05:10,251
acceptable quality, and ordered a
full refund of the purchase price.

113
00:05:10,301 --> 00:05:11,871
The dealer didn't accept that.

114
00:05:11,921 --> 00:05:13,251
It challenged the decision.

115
00:05:13,301 --> 00:05:15,871
And the Supreme Court of
Victoria backed the buyer.

116
00:05:15,921 --> 00:05:18,691
A full refund confirmed by
the state's highest court.

117
00:05:18,741 --> 00:05:21,631
Then, in January 2026,

118
00:05:21,681 --> 00:05:23,691
another buyer won against the same dealer,

119
00:05:23,741 --> 00:05:26,891
this time over the cost of
repairs on a second-hand car.

120
00:05:26,941 --> 00:05:29,211
And that's an important
point most people miss.

121
00:05:29,261 --> 00:05:32,551
The consumer guarantees don't
only apply to brand-new cars.

122
00:05:32,601 --> 00:05:34,791
If you buy a used car
from a licensed dealer,

123
00:05:34,841 --> 00:05:39,271
it still has to be of acceptable quality
for its age, price and kilometres.

124
00:05:39,321 --> 00:05:41,491
The lesson from both cases is simple.

125
00:05:41,541 --> 00:05:44,451
When a business says no, that
isn't the end of the road.

126
00:05:44,501 --> 00:05:47,841
Tribunals and courts can
and do side with the buyer.

127
00:05:48,629 --> 00:05:51,759
Now let's talk about something every
new car owner in Australia should

128
00:05:51,809 --> 00:05:54,959
understand in 2026: recalls.

129
00:05:55,009 --> 00:05:57,359
Because this year, there
have been a lot of them.

130
00:05:57,409 --> 00:06:03,299
In September, BYD recalled 32,009 Shark
6 utes over possible abnormal wear in

131
00:06:03,349 --> 00:06:04,859
the spare wheel assembly.

132
00:06:04,909 --> 00:06:07,819
Owners were told they could remove
the spare wheel if they wanted to keep

133
00:06:07,869 --> 00:06:09,959
driving while they waited for the fix.

134
00:06:10,009 --> 00:06:16,279
In October, Ford recalled 1,085 Rangers
and Everests from the 2024 to 2026

135
00:06:16,329 --> 00:06:20,739
model years, because the 10.1-inch centre
screen can go blank which means the

136
00:06:20,789 --> 00:06:23,019
reversing camera image may not appear.

137
00:06:23,069 --> 00:06:25,949
That's a real safety risk for
anyone standing behind the car.

138
00:06:25,999 --> 00:06:30,869
Ford also recalled the big F-150
pickup over a fire risk the same month.

139
00:06:30,919 --> 00:06:34,859
CarExpert notes that Ford issues more
recalls in Australia than any other car

140
00:06:34,909 --> 00:06:35,779
maker.

141
00:06:35,829 --> 00:06:39,919
Suzuki's new Fronx small SUV was
halted from sale after a rear seatbelt

142
00:06:39,969 --> 00:06:42,059
failure in ANCAP crash testing.

143
00:06:42,109 --> 00:06:45,079
And Deepal had a stop-sale
order on its E07.

144
00:06:45,129 --> 00:06:45,919
Here's what you need to know.

145
00:06:45,969 --> 00:06:50,139
A recall is the manufacturer admitting
a fault and fixing it for free and

146
00:06:50,189 --> 00:06:51,679
that's the system working.

147
00:06:51,729 --> 00:06:53,679
You should always get recall work done.

148
00:06:53,729 --> 00:06:56,639
But a recall doesn't cancel
your consumer rights.

149
00:06:56,689 --> 00:06:58,819
If the fix can't be done
within a reasonable time,

150
00:06:58,869 --> 00:07:01,719
or the same problem keeps
coming back after the repair,

151
00:07:01,769 --> 00:07:04,539
you may be entitled to more
than just a recall repair.

152
00:07:04,589 --> 00:07:07,859
In some cases, that can mean
a refund or a replacement.

153
00:07:07,909 --> 00:07:10,899
You can check whether your car is affected
on the government's Product Safety

154
00:07:10,949 --> 00:07:14,139
Australia recall website, using
your car's make and model,

155
00:07:14,189 --> 00:07:16,449
or by asking your dealer to run your VIN.

156
00:07:18,363 --> 00:07:21,234
Before we go on have you ever had to
fight a dealer or a car maker over a

157
00:07:21,284 --> 00:07:22,314
faulty car?

158
00:07:22,364 --> 00:07:25,134
Tell me your story in the
comments, and whether you won.

159
00:07:25,184 --> 00:07:28,374
Your experience could help someone
else in the same situation.

160
00:07:28,424 --> 00:07:31,334
And if you want more videos that
actually help Aussie drivers,

161
00:07:31,384 --> 00:07:33,894
hit subscribe and turn on notifications.

162
00:07:33,944 --> 00:07:37,804
Now, let's talk about why
this is still so hard in 2026.

163
00:07:38,694 --> 00:07:41,744
If the law is on your side,
why does it feel impossible?

164
00:07:41,794 --> 00:07:44,411
Because the system around
it is slow and confusing.

165
00:07:44,461 --> 00:07:46,844
In July 2026,

166
00:07:46,894 --> 00:07:50,964
the Australian Automotive Dealer Association
released an independent review of

167
00:07:51,014 --> 00:07:53,644
how the Australian Consumer
Law works for cars,

168
00:07:53,694 --> 00:07:56,444
prepared by Emeritus
Professor Jenny Buchan.

169
00:07:56,494 --> 00:07:57,884
Its conclusion was blunt.

170
00:07:57,934 --> 00:08:02,004
Consumer protections for new vehicles
are no longer delivering fair or timely

171
00:08:02,054 --> 00:08:04,844
outcomes not for owners,
and not for dealers either.

172
00:08:04,894 --> 00:08:09,284
The review found that vague definitions
and unclear procedures are driving up

173
00:08:09,334 --> 00:08:12,064
costs, putting pressure on tribunals and,

174
00:08:12,114 --> 00:08:16,604
most importantly, leaving drivers
without their cars for long periods.

175
00:08:16,654 --> 00:08:20,024
Dealers told the review that workshop
backlogs could stretch six to eight

176
00:08:20,074 --> 00:08:24,004
weeks just to diagnose a problem
especially with electric vehicles.

177
00:08:24,054 --> 00:08:24,884
Not fix it.

178
00:08:24,934 --> 00:08:26,404
Just find out what's wrong.

179
00:08:26,454 --> 00:08:29,064
There's another twist most
buyers don't know about.

180
00:08:29,114 --> 00:08:31,664
When something goes wrong,
you deal with the dealer.

181
00:08:31,714 --> 00:08:33,064
But the dealer didn't build the car.

182
00:08:33,114 --> 00:08:37,304
The dealer association says dealers
often end up carrying the legal risk,

183
00:08:37,354 --> 00:08:39,964
while the manufacturer
stays at arm's length.

184
00:08:40,014 --> 00:08:43,104
So it's calling on the federal
government to force manufacturers to get

185
00:08:43,154 --> 00:08:44,744
involved in disputes earlier.

186
00:08:44,794 --> 00:08:46,504
And it's not just about cars.

187
00:08:46,554 --> 00:08:50,354
A report from the Consumer Policy Research
Centre and the Consumer Action Law

188
00:08:50,404 --> 00:08:54,244
Centre found that making a complaint
about a faulty car can involve up to

189
00:08:54,294 --> 00:08:57,224
sixty steps and that's if
everything goes smoothly.

190
00:08:57,274 --> 00:08:59,174
No wonder so many people give up.

191
00:08:59,838 --> 00:09:02,708
So why should you believe
fighting back actually works?

192
00:09:02,758 --> 00:09:05,468
Because of the case that put the
whole car industry on notice.

193
00:09:05,518 --> 00:09:08,568
Between 2013 and 2017,

194
00:09:08,618 --> 00:09:12,908
nine customers bought new Mazdas that
developed serious, recurring faults.

195
00:09:12,958 --> 00:09:15,688
One car had its engine
replaced three times.

196
00:09:15,738 --> 00:09:18,288
When the owners asked for
refunds or replacements,

197
00:09:18,338 --> 00:09:21,468
Mazda refused, or offered
only part of the money back.

198
00:09:21,518 --> 00:09:24,908
The Australian Competition and Consumer
Commission took Mazda to the Federal

199
00:09:24,958 --> 00:09:25,248
Court.

200
00:09:25,298 --> 00:09:29,368
The court found Mazda had made forty-nine
false or misleading statements to

201
00:09:29,418 --> 00:09:31,508
those customers about their rights.

202
00:09:31,558 --> 00:09:32,948
And in 2024,

203
00:09:32,998 --> 00:09:36,568
Mazda was ordered to pay
$11.5 million in penalties,

204
00:09:36,618 --> 00:09:38,508
plus compensation to the owners.

205
00:09:38,558 --> 00:09:42,028
That case is the reason every car company
in Australia now knows the regulator

206
00:09:42,078 --> 00:09:43,148
is watching.

207
00:09:43,198 --> 00:09:46,488
It's also why you should never accept
a business telling you that a refund is

208
00:09:46,538 --> 00:09:47,948
"not our policy".

209
00:09:47,998 --> 00:09:49,288
Under the consumer law,

210
00:09:49,338 --> 00:09:52,038
a business can't make up its
own rules about your rights.

211
00:09:54,081 --> 00:09:55,909
And here's the good news: the
rules are about to get tougher.

212
00:09:55,959 --> 00:09:57,059
In November 2025,

213
00:09:57,109 --> 00:10:00,989
the state and federal consumer affairs
ministers agreed to strengthen the

214
00:10:01,039 --> 00:10:02,489
consumer guarantees.

215
00:10:02,539 --> 00:10:06,009
The plan includes civil penalties
and expanded enforcement powers for

216
00:10:06,059 --> 00:10:07,809
businesses that don't comply.

217
00:10:07,859 --> 00:10:11,989
Right now, a business that wrongly refuses
a valid claim often just has to pay

218
00:10:12,039 --> 00:10:14,509
up later if the customer
fights hard enough.

219
00:10:14,559 --> 00:10:16,729
Penalties would change
that maths completely.

220
00:10:16,779 --> 00:10:19,349
The ministers also agreed to
strengthen what's called supplier

221
00:10:19,399 --> 00:10:20,609
indemnification.

222
00:10:20,659 --> 00:10:21,869
In plain English,

223
00:10:21,919 --> 00:10:24,969
that means dealers should be able to
recover their costs from the manufacturer

224
00:10:25,019 --> 00:10:26,629
when a car is faulty.

225
00:10:26,679 --> 00:10:27,749
That matters to you,

226
00:10:27,799 --> 00:10:31,909
because a dealer who isn't stuck with
the bill has much less reason to stall.

227
00:10:31,959 --> 00:10:33,809
Treasury is now drafting the new laws,

228
00:10:33,859 --> 00:10:36,829
and there will be another round
of consultation before they pass.

229
00:10:36,879 --> 00:10:38,649
So the changes aren't in force yet.

230
00:10:38,699 --> 00:10:40,329
But the direction is clear.

231
00:10:40,379 --> 00:10:43,749
Refusing to fix a faulty car is going
to get a lot more expensive for the

232
00:10:43,799 --> 00:10:45,059
businesses that do it.

233
00:10:45,736 --> 00:10:49,286
So here's exactly what to do if your
new car turns out to be a lemon.

234
00:10:49,336 --> 00:10:51,986
Step one: document everything.

235
00:10:52,036 --> 00:10:55,906
Every fault, every date, every
service visit, every phone call.

236
00:10:55,956 --> 00:10:58,646
Take photos and videos of
the problem when it happens.

237
00:10:58,696 --> 00:11:00,606
Keep every invoice and job card.

238
00:11:00,656 --> 00:11:02,286
Step two: put it in writing.

239
00:11:02,336 --> 00:11:04,846
Phone calls are easy to forget or deny.

240
00:11:04,896 --> 00:11:05,846
Emails aren't.

241
00:11:05,896 --> 00:11:08,126
A simple trick: after every phone call,

242
00:11:08,176 --> 00:11:10,666
send a short email that
says "as discussed today",

243
00:11:10,716 --> 00:11:11,966
and list what you were told.

244
00:11:12,016 --> 00:11:15,396
If they disagree with your summary,
they have to say so in writing.

245
00:11:15,446 --> 00:11:16,916
Keep a fault diary too.

246
00:11:16,966 --> 00:11:19,666
Note the date, the
kilometres, what happened,

247
00:11:19,716 --> 00:11:21,706
and how long the car was off the road.

248
00:11:21,756 --> 00:11:25,486
If a tribunal ever has to decide whether
a repair took a "reasonable time",

249
00:11:25,536 --> 00:11:29,266
a diary with real dates and real days
without a car is one of the strongest

250
00:11:29,316 --> 00:11:30,881
pieces of evidence you can have.

251
00:11:30,931 --> 00:11:35,186
Step three: contact the dealer and the
car maker's Australian head office at

252
00:11:35,236 --> 00:11:36,146
the same time.

253
00:11:36,196 --> 00:11:37,513
It keeps everyone accountable.

254
00:11:37,563 --> 00:11:40,026
Step four: use the right words.

255
00:11:40,076 --> 00:11:43,326
Say you're making a claim under the
consumer guarantees of the Australian

256
00:11:43,376 --> 00:11:44,486
Consumer Law.

257
00:11:44,536 --> 00:11:46,986
If the fault is serious,
or keeps coming back,

258
00:11:47,036 --> 00:11:50,246
say you believe it's a major failure
and you're requesting a refund or a

259
00:11:50,296 --> 00:11:50,886
replacement.

260
00:11:50,936 --> 00:11:53,446
Step five: know what they can't do.

261
00:11:53,496 --> 00:11:56,006
They can't charge you to
fix a fault the law covers.

262
00:11:56,056 --> 00:11:59,226
You don't have to pay anything
towards the remedy you're entitled to.

263
00:11:59,276 --> 00:12:01,746
And your warranty doesn't
replace your consumer rights.

264
00:12:01,796 --> 00:12:03,366
And here's a myth worth busting.

265
00:12:03,416 --> 00:12:06,966
A survey found that around forty per
cent of new car owners believe they have

266
00:12:07,016 --> 00:12:10,606
to service their car at the dealer to
keep their consumer guarantee rights.

267
00:12:10,656 --> 00:12:11,386
You don't.

268
00:12:11,436 --> 00:12:14,926
Using a qualified independent mechanic
who follows the logbook with the right

269
00:12:14,976 --> 00:12:17,446
parts doesn't cancel your rights.

270
00:12:17,496 --> 00:12:21,786
Step six: if you get nowhere, contact
your state's fair trading agency.

271
00:12:21,836 --> 00:12:22,726
If that fails,

272
00:12:22,776 --> 00:12:26,566
take it to your state tribunal
NCAT in New South Wales,

273
00:12:26,616 --> 00:12:31,386
VCAT in Victoria, QCAT in Queensland,
or the equivalent where you live.

274
00:12:31,436 --> 00:12:35,026
Tribunal fees are usually modest, and
you don't need a lawyer for most claims.

275
00:12:35,076 --> 00:12:38,326
You can also report the
business to the ACCC.

276
00:12:38,376 --> 00:12:40,886
And while you're waiting,
don't forget your costs.

277
00:12:40,936 --> 00:12:42,276
Under the Australian Consumer Law,

278
00:12:42,326 --> 00:12:45,806
you can also be entitled to compensation
for losses that were reasonably

279
00:12:45,856 --> 00:12:47,666
foreseeable because of the fault.

280
00:12:47,716 --> 00:12:49,166
That can include things like towing,

281
00:12:49,216 --> 00:12:53,566
or a hire car if you genuinely needed
one while yours was off the road.

282
00:12:53,616 --> 00:12:56,306
Keep every receipt, and include
them in your written claim.

283
00:12:56,356 --> 00:12:59,106
It also helps to be specific
about what you want.

284
00:12:59,156 --> 00:13:00,746
Don't just say "fix it".

285
00:13:00,796 --> 00:13:02,606
Say whether you're asking for a repair,

286
00:13:02,656 --> 00:13:04,006
a refund or a replacement,

287
00:13:04,056 --> 00:13:08,026
give a reasonable deadline say
fourteen days for a written reply,

288
00:13:08,076 --> 00:13:10,486
and ask for the job card from every visit,

289
00:13:10,536 --> 00:13:13,006
showing what was found and what was done.

290
00:13:13,056 --> 00:13:16,106
Businesses respond differently when
they can see you know the process and

291
00:13:16,156 --> 00:13:17,446
you're keeping records.

292
00:13:17,496 --> 00:13:21,196
And one more tip from the BYD
case: don't be afraid to go public.

293
00:13:21,246 --> 00:13:24,856
Owners who spoke to journalists
saw the offer improve within weeks.

294
00:13:25,734 --> 00:13:30,344
Finally, let's talk about the hidden
cost of a faulty car: resale value.

295
00:13:30,394 --> 00:13:31,924
As the BYD case showed,

296
00:13:31,974 --> 00:13:35,524
even a paperwork problem can knock
thousands off what a car is worth.

297
00:13:35,574 --> 00:13:38,184
A car with a history of major
faults can be harder to sell,

298
00:13:38,234 --> 00:13:41,444
and buyers will use every
problem as a bargaining chip.

299
00:13:41,494 --> 00:13:44,324
So if you're dealing with a faulty
car, think about the end game.

300
00:13:44,374 --> 00:13:46,184
A repair might fix today's problem,

301
00:13:46,234 --> 00:13:49,924
but a refund or a replacement may
protect you from losing money later.

302
00:13:49,974 --> 00:13:53,464
And if you're offered compensation,
ask how the amount was worked out.

303
00:13:53,514 --> 00:13:57,124
BYD itself said it raised its payment
after checking reputable valuation

304
00:13:57,174 --> 00:13:57,904
guides.

305
00:13:57,954 --> 00:14:00,404
You're allowed to ask
for that same evidence.

306
00:14:00,454 --> 00:14:03,524
And there's a lesson here for
anyone buying a car right now.

307
00:14:03,574 --> 00:14:06,264
Before you sign, check the build
date on the compliance plate,

308
00:14:06,314 --> 00:14:08,444
not just the model year on the contract.

309
00:14:08,494 --> 00:14:12,444
Ask the dealer to confirm in writing
that the car has no outstanding recalls.

310
00:14:12,494 --> 00:14:14,024
And if you're buying second-hand,

311
00:14:14,074 --> 00:14:17,444
run a check on the national register to
make sure there's no money owing on it

312
00:14:17,494 --> 00:14:18,864
and that it hasn't been written off.

313
00:14:18,914 --> 00:14:22,224
Five minutes of checking before you
buy can save you months of fighting

314
00:14:22,274 --> 00:14:23,074
afterwards.

315
00:14:23,945 --> 00:14:27,935
So, are Aussies fighting back
against faulty new cars in 2026?

316
00:14:27,985 --> 00:14:28,705
Absolutely.

317
00:14:28,755 --> 00:14:31,735
BYD owners more than
tripled their compensation.

318
00:14:31,785 --> 00:14:35,115
A Victorian buyer won a full
refund in the Supreme Court.

319
00:14:35,165 --> 00:14:36,775
And new penalties are on the way.

320
00:14:36,825 --> 00:14:37,915
The system is slow,

321
00:14:37,965 --> 00:14:41,495
but the law is on your side and the
companies that ignore it are paying for

322
00:14:41,545 --> 00:14:42,115
it.

323
00:14:42,165 --> 00:14:43,595
If this video helped you,

324
00:14:43,645 --> 00:14:46,475
share it with someone who's about
to buy a new car it could save them

325
00:14:46,525 --> 00:14:47,295
thousands.

326
00:14:47,345 --> 00:14:50,395
Hit like, subscribe, and tell me
your lemon story in the comments.

327
00:14:50,445 --> 00:14:52,375
And in the next video:

328
00:14:52,425 --> 00:14:55,475
thousands of Aussies paid a deposit for
one of the most hyped vehicles on the

329
00:14:55,525 --> 00:14:57,715
planet and nearly seven years later,

330
00:14:57,765 --> 00:14:59,935
Tesla has just told
them it's never coming.

331
00:14:59,985 --> 00:15:00,785
See you there.
